          "guid": "mszim2g7pwav41rw",
          "message": {
            "text": "The onMount cleanup runs FIRST in tearDown — before disposeMount() and replaceChildren() — so a widget can tear itself down while its node is still attached.\n\nThe whole point of onMount returning a disposer is synchronous, deterministic teardown: onMount typically returns imperative(node, setup)'s disposer, and running it before the DOM is cleared means the widget's teardown fires on a still-connected node, with no dependence on imperative's MutationObserver (which would fire a microtask later, after replaceChildren removed the node). The integration test \"onMount binds a widget with imperative() … synchronously, via the returned disposer\" pins the exact order — setup:a → teardown:a → setup:b → teardown:b, all synchronous. If the cleanup ran after replaceChildren, that teardown would still happen (via the observer) but a frame later and out of this deterministic order, and any teardown that reads the live DOM would find it already detached.\n",
            "markdown": "The onMount cleanup runs FIRST in tearDown — before `disposeMount()` and `replaceChildren()` — so a widget can tear itself down while its node is still attached.\n\nThe whole point of `onMount` returning a disposer is synchronous, deterministic teardown: `onMount` typically returns `imperative(node, setup)`'s disposer, and running it before the DOM is cleared means the widget's teardown fires on a still-connected node, with no dependence on `imperative`'s `MutationObserver` (which would fire a microtask later, after `replaceChildren` removed the node). The integration test \"onMount binds a widget with imperative() … synchronously, via the returned disposer\" pins the exact order — `setup:a → teardown:a → setup:b → teardown:b`, all synchronous. If the cleanup ran after `replaceChildren`, that teardown would still happen (via the observer) but a frame later and out of this deterministic order, and any teardown that reads the live DOM would find it already detached.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/remount.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 64,
                  "endLine": 77,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  function tearDown(): void {\n    // Run the onMount cleanup BEFORE tearing down the DOM, so a synchronous\n    // teardown (e.g. an imperative() disposer returned from onMount) fires while\n    // its node is still attached.\n    if (onMountCleanup !== undefined) {\n      onMountCleanup();\n      onMountCleanup = undefined;\n    }\n    if (disposeMount !== undefined) {\n      disposeMount();\n      disposeMount = undefined;\n    }\n    // Owning parent's children: clear whatever the old mount left so widgets\n    // under it see a real removal (their MutationObserver teardown fires)."
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
